  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Consider the following function fff, defined on pairs of boolean values:\n\nf(x,y)={1,&nbsp;if&nbsp;x=y=00,&nbsp;otherwisef(x, y) = \\begin{cases}\n1, \\text{ if } x = y = 0 \\\\\n0, \\text{ otherwise}\n\\end{cases}f(x,y)={1,&nbsp;if&nbsp;x=y=00,&nbsp;otherwise​So f(0,0)=1f(0, 0) = 1f(0,0)=1, and for any other input f(x,y)=0f(x, y) = 0f(x,y)=0.\n\nYou're given a binary string SSS of length NNN. You can perform the following operation on it:\n\n\nChoose an index iii (1&lt;i&lt;N1 \\lt i \\lt N1&lt;i&lt;N) and do **both**:\n\nSet Si−1=f(Si−1,Si)S_{i-1} = f(S_{i-1}, S_i)Si−1​=f(Si−1​,Si​)\nSet Si+1=f(Si+1,Si)S_{i+1} = f(S_{i+1}, S_i)Si+1​=f(Si+1​,Si​)\n\n\nFind the **maximum** possible number of ones that SSS can have after performing several such operations (possibly, none).\n\nAlso, find a sequence of at most 3N3N3N operations that attains this maximum.\n\nIt can be proved that such a sequence always exists.\n\nNote that you do not have to minimize the number of operations.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT — the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the length of the string.\nThe second line of each test case contains the binary string SSS.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output two lines:\n\n\n\nOn the first line, print a single integer KKK (0≤K≤3N0 \\leq K \\leq 3N0≤K≤3N): the number of moves you are going to make.\nOn the second line, print KKK space-separated integers i1,i2,…,iKi_1, i_2, \\ldots, i_Ki1​,i2​,…,iK​, denoting the indices chosen by you to perform the operation, in sequence.\n\nEach of these indices should be &gt;1\\gt 1&gt;1 and &lt;N\\lt N&lt;N.\n\nNote that if K=0K = 0K=0, you may either leave the second line blank, or choose to skip it entirely.\n\n\nIf there are multiple valid outputs, you may print any of them.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "3≤N≤3⋅1053 \\leq N \\leq 3\\cdot 10^53≤N≤3⋅105",
      "SSS is a binary string, i.e, contains only the characters `0` and `1`.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 3⋅1053\\cdot 10^53⋅105."
    ],
